>Spam-casting? How is it spam?

In this case it just means casting it many times, although doing so
does spam up your message history.

For those who don't know, haste self has no maximum duration. Casting
it makes you very fast (as fast as intrinsic speed + boots of speed)
for 100 to 109 (more) turns, or 160 to 169 if skilled or expert in
escape. So if you have 90 mana and you cast haste self successfully 6
times (at 15 mana a cast) you will speed up for about 600 turns or
about 960 if skilled/expert.

This can be very handy as you can now wear water walking, kicking,
jumping or levitation boots and still be very fast. Jumping + being
very fast is very nice to have on the run.


As for the ascension kit you might also consider:
* a helm of opposite alignment, which gives 2/3 chance you will get to
an altar you can ascend with first
* wands of polymorph, slow monster or opening to deal with plane of air
* wands of teleport for astral, both to zap monsters away or break
should you become surrounded by, say, multiple archons
* oilskin cloak or amulet of magical breathing for plane of water
* if you've managed to save any, royal jelly provides 200 nutrition in
1 turn, and only weighs 2. for comparison k-rations provide 400 in one
turn, but weigh 10. if carrying around 10-20 for fighting vs. famine
royal jelly will save you a lot of weight.

Everything else I can think of has already been mentioned.



